              "text": "गैलो (gailo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from grahila, \"possessed by an evil spirit\". CDIAL lists Marwari gahalo under it (CDIAL 4366). The Marwari row means \"foolish\"; गैलो (gailo) has lost its h. CDIAL thinks the Sanskrit word was made from Middle Indo-Aryan gahila, built on graha, \"seizing\"."
